<article class="env-lemma" id="09UP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09UP">Lemma <span data-tag="09UP">37.59.13</span>.</a> Let $X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes which is locally of finite type. Let $m \in \mathbf{Z}$. Let $\mathcal{F}^\bullet $ be a (locally) bounded above complex of $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules such that $\mathcal{F}^ i$ is $(m - i)$-pseudo-coherent relative to $S$ for all $i$. Then $\mathcal{F}^\bullet $ is $m$-pseudo-coherent relative to $S$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows from Cohomology, Lemma <a href="/tag/09V7" data-tag="09V7">20.47.7</a> and the definitions. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>